[Positive-probability sequences] By mutual independence [F1], $\mathbb P(O_{k}=a_{k}	ext{ for every }k)=\prod_{k}
u(a_{k})$, a product of positive numbers; the failure event $\{(O_{1},\dots,O_{N})
otin C\}$ contains the complementary event of this outcome and is disjoint from it, so [F2] bounds its probability below by $\prod_{k}
u(a_{k})$; the constant sequence is the special case. This proves (b). [given, F1, F2, algebra]
